          "message": {
            "text": "POST /user/avatar/{user}: Unrestricted file upload supported by source analysis [confirmed_vulnerability]. A client upload is stored by UploadedFile::move. Stored name: mixed; extension: client; destination served: yes. No server-side type control precedes the write. Generate the name and allow-list or verify the type on the server; this practice finding stands even before exploitability is judged. Upload assessment: type restriction none, exposure served_executable, coverage incomplete. Scanner policy: The stored file keeps a client-chosen extension, no server-side type control precedes the UploadedFile::move write, and the destination is under the document root, so an uploaded executable file can be requested (CWE-434). This is a static judgment, not runtime exploitation."
          },
